// New Loop Plus talents file. Changes apply the next time the game starts.
//
// Every entry below starts switched off. Set "enabled": true on a talent to add it to the loop rewards.
// Delete this file to get the defaults back.
//
// A talent entry:
//   "id"          the talent ID (row IDs are id * 10 + level, so at most 9 levels)
//   "enabled"     true or false; a switched-off entry changes nothing, its buffs and effects included
//   "copyFrom"    for a new talent ID: the talent whose rows it starts from
//   "name", "description", "levelText"   text, either "plain" or { "en": "...", "zh": "..." }
//   "fields"      any Config_Talent field for every level, such as { "ShowType": 2 }
//   "levels"      one { } per level: "cost", "buff", "description", "levelText", "fields".
//                 More levels than the game has adds levels; fewer hides the rest.
//   "buffs", "effects"   Config_Buff and Config_Effect rows this talent changes or makes (see below)
//   "reinforce"   { "talentBuff": A, "doorWindowBuff": B }: while the owner has buff A, every home door
//                 and window gets buff B
//
// A buff or effect entry: "id", an optional "copyFrom" (needed to make a new row), and "fields",
// named as the game's tables name them (ConfigName, IntValue0, BuffSatietyDel, EffectConfigId...).
// The "buffs" and "effects" lists at the bottom always apply.
{
  "talents": [
    // Cut talents that work as the game left them.
    { "id": 1006, "enabled": false },  // Driver: buy vehicles, shorter travel time
    { "id": 2017, "enabled": false },  // No-Till Soil: replant without tilling
    { "id": 3076, "enabled": false },  // Trailblazer: Planning Points for each crisis overcome
    { "id": 4004, "enabled": false },  // Liaison (endless): three camps call for aid once more
    { "id": 4006, "enabled": false },  // Radio Station (endless): aid requests announced a day early

